Because the overall variance of time-series data can also be biased by undersampling or parasitic noise, the thermally calibrated value of k is, in practice, obtained by fitting the PSD (Sxx) of the freely fluctuating cantilever to the expected Lorentzian functional form of a damped harmonic oscillator: [15, 16, 23]
